        "id": "p26-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Approximate $\\displaystyle\\int_2^{10} f(x)\\,dx$ by calculating the areas of two trapezia and then adding.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$164$",
          "worked": "First trapezium: $\\dfrac12(12+20)(4)=64$.\n\nSecond trapezium: $\\dfrac12(20+30)(4)=100$.\n\nTotal: $64+100=164$.\n\nTherefore $\\displaystyle\\int_2^{10}f(x)\\,dx\\approx164$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Check your answer to part a by using the formula for the trapezoidal rule.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$164$, agreeing with part a.",
          "worked": "$h=6-2=4$. Using the trapezoidal rule:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int_2^{10}f(x)\\,dx&\\approx\\frac42\\bigl(12+2(20)+30\\bigr)\\\\&=164.\\end{align*}$$\nThis agrees with part a.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 19
      }
